PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
The key target is the isolated white pair at (2,6) and (3,6), whose liberties are (1,6), (2,5), (3,5), and (4,6). Black’s left/central group around (3,4)/(4,4) has liberties (1,4), (2,4), (3,5), (4,5). Black’s right/lower group around c7 and (5,5)/(5,6) has only liberties (1,6), (4,6), (4,5), so (4,5) is the connecting point between the two black groups.

Public responses are split: (4,5) was proposed by colleagues 1, 3, 4, 15; (3,5) by 2, 5, 8, 9, 11, 13, 14; (2,5) by 7, 16, 18; both (2,5),(3,5) by 10, 12; and (2,4),(2,5) by 17. Colleague 6 gave no answer.

My current leaning is that the correct two answers are (2,5) and (3,5), in lexicographic order. These are the two left-side liberties of the white pair and directly reduce/capture the two white stones. (4,5) is important for connecting Black’s groups, but it does not directly reduce the white pair’s liberties, and White may be able to extend at (2,5) or use (1,5) to create a liberty race. (2,4) appears not to attack the white pair directly and has weaker support.

Unresolved/needs confirmation: verify that (3,5) truly works if White responds at (2,5); verify that (4,5) alone cannot force the capture; confirm whether the expected final answer is exactly (2,5), (3,5) or if (4,5) is also considered correct by the puzzle.
}

